    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406-a2">

                <pb facs="0543" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg463"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Lemly to Mr.
                            Long.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Board of Examination of Steel Floating Dry Dock,<lb/>United States
                                Naval Station</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Habana,
                            Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-01-19"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 19,
                    1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the work of the board of which
                    I am senior member, appointed by the Department’s order of the 21st ultimo, No.
                    245413, for the purpose of examining into and reporting upon the condition of
                    the steel floating dry dock, the property of the Spanish government, located in
                    the harbor of Habana, Cuba, I am directed by said board to invite the
                    Department’s attention to the courteous and able manner in which Capt. Pedro del
                    Peral, of the Spanish navy, in charge of the structure, has facilitated our
                    labors (this day concluded) in each and every particular.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sam. C. Lemly</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain and Judge-Advocate-General, U. S.
                        Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
